            <ArticleTitle>Methadone as a rescue for failed high-dose opiate therapy for catastrophic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>138-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Methadone is a unique opioid with several special properties besides being a mu agonist, which makes for difficulty in the calculation of equianalgesic doses. A series of three cases is presented to illustrate this point.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
